3. Section A – Feature Selection

Section A focuses on identifying features suitable for downstream rule construction.

The objective is to establish a feature set demonstrating predictive capability while maintaining logical consistency, explainability, and governance readiness.

The feature selection process consists of:

* Statistical analysis
* Machine learning evaluation
* Explainability assessment
* Logic validation
* Human validation

⸻

3.1 Information Value Analysis

Information Value (IV) analysis is applied as the initial screening stage to assess predictive capability independently for each feature.

IV metrics provide an initial indication of variable strength and support early feature prioritisation.

Features failing to satisfy predefined thresholds may subsequently be excluded from downstream analysis.

Outputs generated during this stage include:

* Feature ranking tables
* IV summaries
* Visual ranking plots

These outputs provide an initial understanding of predictive performance across the feature space.

