3.2 Correlation Analysis

Correlation analysis is subsequently performed to evaluate relationships between predictor variables and target outcomes as well as relationships among predictor variables themselves.

Feature-to-target analysis provides an initial understanding of variable influence on risk outcomes.

Feature-to-feature analysis identifies:

* Redundant predictors
* High correlation structures
* Potential multicollinearity

Heatmap visualisations are generated to support interpretation and feature refinement activities.

This process reduces duplicated information and supports subsequent feature selection.

