3.4 Machine Learning Evaluation

Following statistical analysis, PRAISE incorporates machine learning evaluation to further assess feature performance.

The current implementation applies XGBoost models.

XGBoost was selected due to:

* Strong predictive performance
* Flexible feature handling capability
* Support for monotonic constraints

Monotonic constraints preserve logical relationships between predictor variables and outcomes, improving interpretability and governance alignment.

Feature selection remains iterative throughout this process.

Candidate features may be refined according to:

* Information Value performance
* Worst-tail analysis
* Feature importance
* Expert judgement

This stage supports identification of predictive and stable signals for downstream rule construction.

