4. Section B – Rule Construction

Section B focuses on transforming selected features into executable rule structures.

Features identified during Section A may be directly utilised or manually defined for downstream rule generation.

The rule construction process incorporates:

* Search space definition
* Governance constraints
* Rule optimisation
* Performance evaluation

⸻

4.1 Search Space Definition

Rule generation begins with search space construction.

Search ranges may be derived from:

* Feature dictionaries
* User-defined configurations
* Valid ranges
* Direction constraints

Earlier logic validation activities ensure that generated rules remain intuitive and aligned with expected behaviour.

